{"task": "IG-2B05", "path": "docs/IG-WGU-ARCHITECTURE.md", "start_line": 99, "lines": ["## Complete sources and reconciliation", "", "Inventory all 44 PDF pages independently of the KB: headings, clauses, notes, examples,", "tables, legends, diagrams, and editorial regions. Keep PDF page number separate from", "printed labels. Text extraction is a helper; diagrams and meaningful decorations need", "image evidence. Every region is represented, partially represented, a gap, or excluded", "with a reason. Gaps never count as represented content.", "", "Reconcile all imported records: exact/partial match, contradiction, missing KB content,", "missing source, or possible duplicate. Preserve KB bytes, candidate interpretations,", "evidence, and corrections separately. Cross-chapter exceptions and external tables", "remain explicit dependencies. A table assembled by KB authors can cite multiple clauses;", "do not invent a single publisher region for it.", "", "Each profile pins edition, mode, options, scenario, source revisions and compatibility", "decisions. A 2018 4E scenario book does not inherit 5E authority from the KB manifest.", "Do not invent universal 'newer wins' or 'more specific wins' precedence. Unofficial", "aids remain secondary material. An empty errata list is not proof that no errata exist.", "", "## Revision, review and updates", "", "One logical source IG links to one formal semantic representation; the executable", "package is derived and immutable. All operations map back to exact clause/evidence", "revisions. Do not maintain three independent hand-edited descriptions of a rule.", "", "Review records pin target revision/aspect, evidence, profile and dependencies.", "Technical checks, source/meaning review, and human acceptance are separate. Model", "observations cannot grant semantic acceptance. Incomplete review bases imply unknown", "freshness; changed bases imply stale. Acceptance is never inherited by a changed aspect.", "", "Updates compare old WGU, new WGU and current WGC. Deletion in WGU retires provenance,", "not IG history. Recompute impact through reads/writes, triggers, bindings, table/profile", "dependencies and unresolved references. Preserve decisions; request new ones for affected", "meaning. Rebuild packages and replay regressions before promoting an updated profile.", "", "## Product readiness", "", "Report input accounting, source coverage at each representation level, current human", "acceptance, resolved dependencies, compiled scope, and gameplay readiness separately.", "Opaque text is valid in a working source IG. If it affects legal choices, timing,", "visibility, costs or effects, it blocks executable readiness of the dependent scope.", "Unknown conditions cannot be assumed inactive to bypass a dependency.", ""], "truncated": true}

